step Get Runecloth
  when knows 18449
  tip 2590 Runecloth for Tailoring 265-300: 74 Runecloth Shoulders. Humanoids of level 45-60 drop it, and what you loot as you level counts. The arrow takes you to the best farm for your level: mobs at or below it first, then the most Runecloth per minute and the nearest; it picks again as you level. The guide window shows the kills and minutes it takes there and a second choice. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 14047 x2590 nearest gather levels 45-60
  auction 14047 x2590

step Get Ironweb Spider Silk
  when knows 18449
  tip 148 Ironweb Spider Silk for Tailoring 265-300: 74 Runecloth Shoulders. Ironweb Spider Silk drops most from Plague Lurker, Rock Stalker and Searing Lava Spider, among others. The arrow takes you to the best farm for your level: mobs at or below it first, then the most Ironweb Spider Silk per minute and the nearest; it picks again as you level. The guide window shows the kills and minutes it takes there and a second choice. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 14227 x148 nearest gather levels 45-59
  auction 14227 x148

step Runecloth Shoulders to 300
  when knows 18449
  tip Runecloth Shoulders is orange at 265 (yellow 275, green 290, grey 305): about 62 crafts to 300, up to 74 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 7 Bolt of Runecloth, 2 Ironweb Spider Silk, 4 Rugged Leather and 1 Rune Thread. Make the 434 Bolt of Runecloth first. Its pattern (Pattern: Runecloth Shoulders) drops from mobs all over the world and does not bind: buy it at the Auction House. Seven bolts, two Ironweb Spider Silk and four Rugged Leather a craft: the dearest stretch. The spiders of Western Plaguelands and Silithus drop the silk (the marked spots), or the Auction House. Tailoring 300 is a Legacy System milestone. If you got here without learning Bolt of Runecloth, learn it now: an earlier step teaches it.
  learn 18401 npc 11052 only Alliance
  learn 18401 npc 2399 only Horde map 1424
  craft 18401 x434
  craft 18449 until 300
  skill Tailoring 300

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Artisan, without the pattern (265-300)
section Tailoring 265-300

step Tailoring 265-300: vendor goods
  when !knows 18449
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 100 Rune Thread (50g); about 50g in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Alexandra Bolero and Jillian Tanner; Orgrimmar: Borya and Tamar).
  buy 14341 x100 nearest

step Pattern: Runecloth Boots
  when !knows 18449
  tip Pattern: Runecloth Boots teaches Runecloth Boots (Tailoring 235) for 2g. Sold by Darnall (Moonglade), limited stock. Its sellers keep one or two in stock that come back some time after a sale; it binds when picked up, so the Auction House never has it.
  buy 14488 nearest

step Get Rugged Leather
  when !knows 18449
  tip 588 Rugged Leather for Tailoring 265-300: 147 Runecloth Boots. Skinning: beasts of level 48-60. The arrow takes the Skinning loop that gets you them soonest from where you are and walks it until your bags hold them; the window names the loop, its lap and the laps left. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 8170 x588 gather Skinning 225
  loop Un'Goro Crater lvl 55 lap 1371 yield 30.8 r 80 at 67.4,15.5 69.1,17.6 70.7,21.4 68.3,21.3 62.5,17.6 64.9,16.8
